// @run
// @log 7
// @log 3
// @log 5
// Regression (silent-class-inventory D244), and the NO-TWIN file of the pair — a twin is a
// whole-program property, so the two twin states need two files and this one declares no
// standalone struct of `Circle`'s layout at all. Cell 1 is the generated cell `p00192` of
// `scripts/silent-sweep/d243/genbox.py --block P`, `check-clean invalid wasm` on `322c07f2`
// with NOTHING annotated anywhere in the program.
//
// `globalKind`'s `ObjLit` arm gave a module GLOBAL the union BOX (kind 4) wherever the
// struct table had no row for the shape and a union was declared. `collectLocals` has asked
// a different question there since D51 — `structIndexOfLet < 0 && letObjLitVariantIdx >= 0`
// is the kind-8 bare ARM — and `criClassify`'s return rung asks it of a function result. The
// module global asked neither, so the SAME six characters repped two different ways at two
// storage classes, and the list literal beside it (whose element the checker typed as the
// arm `Circle`) built an `(array (mut (ref null $uVarHeap[Circle])))` that `array.new_fixed`
// then pushed the box into: `vl check` rc 0, and the engine refuses the module.
//
// CELL 2 IS THE AXIS, and it is why the earlier grids could not see this: the identical
// binding inside a `function` has always RUN. Every cell of the list-container block that
// found D184 was `escope=mod`, so the pair that discriminates was never generated.
//
// CELL 3 IS THE SAME ROOT WEARING THE LOUD DISGUISE — a bare field read of the boxed global
// was `emitProgram: field access but no struct type declared`, because the box has no struct
// layout to read a field from. One root, two outcomes, which is why the loud half was not
// evidence the silent half was absent.
//
// WHERE A LAYOUT TWIN IS DECLARED NOTHING MOVES, and that is D39's ruling rather than an
// omission: `structIndexOfObj` then answers before this rung and the global stays a `struct`
// cell, which is the right answer for an un-annotated literal with a struct claimant.
type Circle = { r: i32 }
type Sq = { s: i32 }
type Shape = Circle | Sq

const iv = { r: 7 }
const c = [iv]
if (c)[0].r == 7 { print(7) } else { print(0) }

function rd() {
  const ivf = { r: 3 }
  const cf = [ivf]
  if (cf)[0].r == 3 { print(3) } else { print(0) }
}
rd()

const bare = { r: 5 }
print(bare.r)
